---
// A post page's text and picture (Feature 006 #147; spec #144 "Post pages: News, Activity and
// Health Content"). From lg a post with a picture reads in two columns ("สองคอลัมน์"): the left
// column holds what the page has, in its order, and the right column, 28 rem wide, holds the
// picture whole with a "เปิดภาพขนาดเต็ม" link to its file. Below lg the parts read in one column in
// the page's order: the default slot (the header, and an Activity's details), the picture and its
// link, then the `body` slot (a body, its source and its topics). The link shows at every width,
// as a phone needs it most (Product Owner, 2026-11-04: #147 comment 6634124888). A post without a
// picture keeps one column.
//
// The picture stays in view while the left column scrolls ("ลอยตาม (แนะนำ)") and stops at the end
// of the two columns: a grid item's grid area is its containing block (CSS Grid Layout 1, "Placing
// Grid Items"), which a sticky box never leaves (CSS Positioned Layout 3, sticky positioning), and
// the picture's spans every row of the block (observed with Playwright 1.63.0's Chromium;
// tests/browser/public-posts.spec.ts checks it). So what a page puts after this block, such as an
// Activity's photos, comes below the picture and never under it (the Product Owner's finding of
// 2026-11-04, spec #144). With a `body` slot the block has two rows: the first takes the height of
// what it holds, and the picture's extra height goes to the second, a flexible row (CSS Grid
// Layout 1's track sizing), so the body stays right under the header when the picture is the
// taller. Without one the block has a single row, so no empty row and its gap lengthen it past the
// text. A `body` slot that renders nothing counts as none, so a News or Health Content post with
// no body, source or topics (PostBody.astro) ends with the last part it shows, with no empty row or
// gap after it (#198; #190 comment 6707205912, Empty Post page row B). `Astro.slots.has` tells
// only that a page passed the slot (astro 7.3.5 dist/core/render/slots.js), so the block renders
// it once with `Astro.slots.render` and places that HTML. The picture follows only while the left
// column is the longer, and one taller than the window shows its lower part as the block ends. The
// Product Owner kept both limits (2026-11-04: #147 comment 6634124888).
//
// The picture fills the column's width at its own aspect ratio, never cropped, in a box shaped by
// the size EmDash keeps with the image (docs/agents/emdash-1.1.0.md "Media" says how), so a
// dominant colour EmDash's Image paints behind it never shows beside it (#147 comment 6628040681;
// its blurhash placeholder does not show at all, same section). It
// loads at once with a high fetch priority, since from lg it is in view when the page opens
// (emdash 1.1.0 src/components/EmDashImage.astro). The link opens the file as it was uploaded,
// which EmDash stores unchanged (src/astro/routes/api/media.ts), whatever rendition the picture
// shows (ADR 0003), so a citizen can read a One Page's small print (#144 user story 17). It is an
// onward link on this site, so it ends in chevron-right (ArrowLink.astro).
import { Image } from "emdash/ui";
import { availableMedia, mediaFileHref } from "../lib/media";
import type { ImageFieldValue } from "../lib/news";
import ArrowLink from "./ArrowLink.astro";

interface Props {
	/** The post's picture, its featured image field's value. */
	image: ImageFieldValue | null | undefined;
}

/** The picture's width: the right column from lg, the reading width below it. */
const PICTURE_SIZES = "(min-width: 64rem) 28rem, (min-width: 48rem) 48rem, 100vw";

const image = await availableMedia(Astro.props.image, Astro.locals.emdash);
const fullSizeHref = image && mediaFileHref(image, Astro.locals.emdash);
const bodyHtml = await Astro.slots.render("body");
const showsBody = Boolean(bodyHtml?.trim());
---

<div
	class:list={[
		"flex flex-col gap-8",
		image && "lg:grid lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1fr)_28rem] lg:items-start lg:gap-x-12",
		image && showsBody && "lg:grid-rows-[auto_1fr]",
	]}
>
	<div class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:col-start-1">
		<slot />
	</div>
	{image && (
		<div
			class:list={[
				"flex flex-col gap-2 lg:sticky lg:top-[calc(var(--header-offset)+1.5rem)] lg:col-start-2 lg:row-start-1",
				showsBody && "lg:row-span-2",
			]}
		>
			<Image
				image={image}
				priority
				sizes={PICTURE_SIZES}
				class="h-auto w-full max-w-3xl rounded-24 bg-surface-soft"
			/>
			{fullSizeHref && <ArrowLink href={fullSizeHref}>เปิดภาพขนาดเต็ม</ArrowLink>}
		</div>
	)}
	{showsBody && (
		<div class="lg:col-start-1">
			<Fragment set:html={bodyHtml} />
		</div>
	)}
</div>
